            <div class="about__content markdown">
                <h2>What I Like Exploring</h2>
                <p>Maverick Times will keep changing as I discover new things, but these are the areas I naturally keep coming back to:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>SEO & websites:</strong> Testing ideas, studying search results, improving websites and seeing what actually brings organic traffic.</li>
                    <li><strong>Startups & business:</strong> Following interesting companies, new products, business models and ideas that are gaining attention.</li>
                    <li><strong>Marketing:</strong> Breaking down campaigns, growth strategies, content ideas and the small things that make a business stand out.</li>
                    <li><strong>Warangal & Telangana:</strong> Writing practical guides about places, local businesses, travel, food and things happening around the city.</li>
                    <li><strong>Food:</strong> Trying local restaurants, cafés and street food and sharing what I actually found rather than copying a generic list from the internet.</li>
                    <li><strong>Technology:</strong> Building things, experimenting with new tools and learning by actually making projects.</li>
                </ul>

                <h2>Why I Started Maverick Times</h2>
                <p>I like building websites, but I also like the process that happens after a website goes live: finding a topic, researching it, writing about it, improving the page, watching the search data and learning what people actually want to read.</p>
                <p>That is a big part of what I want Maverick Times to be. It is not meant to be a huge publication trying to cover everything. I would rather build a collection of useful, honest and interesting articles around topics I genuinely care about — especially Warangal and the local things I can experience first-hand.</p>

                <h2>Local, But Not Limited to One Topic</h2>
                <p>Warangal is going to be an important part of the site. I want to write about its food, places, businesses, student life, travel and local stories. At the same time, I will continue writing about SEO, websites, startups, marketing and other niche topics when I have something useful to say.</p>
                <p>The goal is simple: <strong>learn, build, test and share what I find.</strong></p>

                <h2>Get in Touch</h2>
